; 01-replay-names-distinct: distinct of one item doesn't bind remove-all's hd and tl, of more items it does (a name
; bound in a call is a local's from then on, and a call named by it takes its general way, which leaves the Site
; there).  The probe (hd v (g)): Op2's fast way (the Site (g)'s code left) while hd is no local's name; then the
; general way's (the call itself).  One call of distinct runs four times, so its code's Site is kept and replayed
(def {hd} +)
(fun {g} {+ 70000 70001})
(fun {p a b} {+ a b})
(fun {probe} {p v v (hd v (g))})
(def {v} 100003)
(probe)
(probe)
(each {x (list {1} {1} {1} {1 2 3})} (distinct x))
(probe)
(probe)
